 },
 "deviations_from_design": [
  "CE-KT World forms (ce_kt_world*) are included although design-v2 section 3 dropped them: the P1 task names them.",
  "Events are typed with g : Fin qAccept x Fin (qCreate + 1) (the codomain of designateIn); sums run over Fin qAccept x Fin qCreate with castSucc.",
  "CE-OR: dirOf route entry is Direction.Receives on the receiving handle; claims are first-entry claims (firstHandle).",
  "CE-UKS: the generic side/witness is realized as the receiver family UksReceiverAt (Server peer receiver) and the sender family UksSenderAt (owner sender), each with a first-entry claim.",
  "CE-LOR: per-target events are the existential events with the claim lorClaim = firstTest (D_g of them is LorElig g / LorWin g by lorElig_target); the bound is ofReal |advantage| <= sum in extended non-negative reals; the final-world fact uses hidingOf and decisionHiding; the Server form puts PeerTests into the events.",
  "slots_close / slots_server are realized per headline (view_unslotted, chance_split, chain_server, server_view) rather than as one generic lemma.",
  "ptc takes its guesser over kem.IND_CCA_oracleSpec (definitionally MlKemCCAOracleSpec); two proofs use set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false.",
  "Commit 68498a95 corrects three documentation strings of the events module (no statement, proof or guard change).",
  "Three proofs use set_option linter.deprecated false for VCVio's deprecated probEvent (Pr[...] notation) only: ptc_random_le, ptc_correct_draws (anomaly), chance_split (LOR); copies without the suppression report only probEvent warnings (fix pass; the two suppressions that hid nothing were removed in 6d13ef8b).",
  "Review fix pass 6d13ef8b: unpublished_final, ce_or_b2s_target, ce_or_b2s, ce_or_s2b_target and ce_or_s2b drop the premise DecoderAgreement route codec.frameRead (strictly stronger: same conclusions under fewer hypotheses); unpublished_final applies PqxdhRecordFactsOriginClosure.idealAuth_unpublished_bound (the third conjunct of origin_statement) instead of origin_statement."
 ],
